Track 3: The Ghost-Sump Recipe
- Story & Context: Now that the mines are sealed, the younger generation tells stories of the Great Subterranean Kitchen where the trapped once sang to the rocks until they crumbled. Tourists bring modern recording gear to the surface of Shaft-Alpha, trying to catch the phantom vibrations of the saxophones still rattling inside the earth. The song is the only map remaining, a menu for a meal no one can ever truly digest. "Dig until the floor turns to sugar and light."
